* TOOL_HOME
* The full-screen toolkit's front end: the home screen (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md section 13, A10).  For everyone; the page differs for the administrator.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 22 Oct 26 dm  New (S.75, H1; the owner: "the display design is approved as drawn. Start home H0, then H1 and H2").
* 23 Oct 26 dm  The AI line (AI line stage 1; $tk_ai): when the AI is on for the account it takes the hint row, is the last stop of the Tab ring, and turns a request into one of
*               the page's tiles or a command to run.  Without the AI there is no change at all.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  The administrator's page has a tile for every administrator page (plan 13.2: a new app adds its row in the commit that builds it): System gains Audit trail and
*               Configuration; People and access (Accounts, Sessions and locks, Gates) and Data, network and AI (Backups, Master files, Remote servers, AI) are new groups, all three
*               side by side in one band so that Tools and Everyone stay on the first screen.  Tiles may carry a live line (accounts, sessions, master files) read when the page is
*               built and every 30 seconds.  The development apps have a group Develop under Everyone (Files, Vocabulary, Dictionary, Queries, Bulk update, Programs, Tests).
* 26 Oct 26 dm  S.75, home: SUB-MENUS (a tile whose action is menu:<name> opens the groups of that menu as a page of their own, with a Back tile at the left of the header, Esc and
*               Backspace going back one, the path on the status line, 8 levels at most and a menu already open refused), and the RECENT GROUP (the tiles the person started last, newest
*               first, when they have turned it on in the View menu; kept by !home_recent in their own file &menus&; off as delivered).  The page is built in two steps now: the whole table,
*               then pick.level keeps the groups of the menu being shown.  Behaviour-preserving while there: reopen and rebuild share enter.level; an empty band takes no room.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   HOME
*
*   A start screen of tiles, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least; a smaller window is refused).  The administrator's page and an account
*   holder's page are built from one table and differ in what is in it; every tile starts a command exactly as the person would type it, so a tile adds no
*   access (the gates apply as at the terminal).
*
*     System     (the administrator only) Menu management, Bypass programs, Audit trail, Configuration
*     People and access, Data network and AI     (the administrator only) Accounts, Sessions and locks, Gates; Backups, Master files, Remote servers, AI.  Each tile starts the page's verb.
*     Develop    the development apps, for every account: Files (tool.files), Vocabulary (tool.voc), Dictionary (tool.dict), Queries (tool.query), Bulk update (tool.bulk), Programs (tool.catalog), Tests (tool.test)
*     Tools      the standard tools of every account: Editor (sed), IDE (ide), Record editor (ced)
*     Everyone   Terminal (leaves the screen for the ordinary prompt; EXIT comes back), Keys (tool.keys)
*     Header     who is signed on and when, Switch account (a pick list of the accounts this person may enter, then the screen of that account) and Sign out
*
*   Recent     (only when the person has turned it on, View menu) the tiles started last, newest first, as the first group of the page
*
*   SUB-MENUS.  A tile whose action is menu:<name> opens a page of its own: the groups of the table that belong to the menu <name> (the sixth value of a group, HG.MENU; the top page's
*   groups have none).  The page has a Back tile at the left of the header (the identity moves right), the status line shows the path (Home > Develop), Esc, Backspace and the Back tile go
*   back one level and give the focus and the scroll back as they were, 8 levels are the most, and a menu that is already open above is refused (no page can open itself).  A menu with no
*   tile (all turned off) has no folder tile.  No tile of the delivered page opens a sub-menu yet: a table that wants one declares a folder tile and gives its groups the menu name.
*
*   The panel under the header scrolls: the page is laid out at its full height and the rows that fit are drawn, with a scroll bar in the last column.  Keys:
*   the arrow keys move to the nearest tile, Tab and Back-tab go in reading order, Home and End to the first and last, Page Up and Page Down by group, a letter
*   to the next tile that begins with it, Enter or the space bar starts the tile, F5 builds the page again, F10 opens the menu bar, Ctrl-Q signs out.  A click
*   starts a tile, the wheel scrolls three rows.  The end of the input ends the program.
*
*   THE AI LINE (only when the AI is on for the account: the gate, a provider, a model and a key; else there is no row and nothing below applies).  It takes the row that holds the
*   hint, after the last tile in the Tab ring (Tab from the last tile, Back-tab from the first), or a click.  Enter on a request shows everything that will be sent and sends nothing
*   until Send; the answer comes in a popup and may propose ONE of this page's tiles (Accept starts it as a click would; Enter alone accepts a tile that only opens a tool) or ONE
*   command (shown; it runs only on Run, as the Terminal would run it).  Sign out and Switch account are never offered.  The model sees the tile names, nothing of the account's data.
*
*   THE NAMED COMMON /TKHOME/: hflag is set when the person left by the Terminal tile (the EXIT verb then comes back to this screen); hlogto is set only
*   while this program runs a LOGTO, so that the sign-on hook (!home_entry) does not start a second screen inside it.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_home
$catalog $tool_home

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

deffun is_grp_member(user, group) calling '!is_grp_member'

$define HT.ID      1       ;* a tile is a field of tl, its values:  the id (for the key jump and the tests)
$define HT.GROUP   2       ;* the group's number in gr
$define HT.LABEL   3
$define HT.GLYPH   4       ;* three cells of ASCII, so that any locale draws it
$define HT.SUB     5       ;* the line under the label
$define HT.ACT     6       ;* cmd:<sentence>, terminal, switch or signout
$define HT.PAL     7       ;* the palette's name
$define HT.SIZE    8       ;* n normal 21 by 5, w wide 43 by 5, s small 21 by 3
$define HT.PAUSE   9       ;* 1 when the command prints lines: wait for a key before the screen comes back
$define HT.WHY     10      ;* null, or why the tile is dimmed (a gate that is off)
$define HT.X       11      ;* the cell of its top left corner: x; y is a row of the panel for a tile in a group and a row of the screen for a header tile
$define HT.Y       12
$define HT.W       13
$define HT.H       14
$define HT.FIXED   15      ;* 1 for a header tile (not scrolled)
$define HT.LIVE    16      ;* null, or the live line shown in place of the sub line (read again when the page opens, on F5 and every 30 seconds)

$define HG.NAME    1       ;* a group is a field of gr, its values
$define HG.BAND    2       ;* the band it stands in: groups of one band stand side by side
$define HG.COLS    3       ;* how many tile columns it is wide (2 or 6)
$define HG.Y       4       ;* the panel row of its heading, set by the layout
$define HG.X       5
$define HG.MENU    6       ;* null for a group of the top page, else the name of the menu (sub-menu page) it belongs to

$define PANEL.TOP  5       ;* the first row of the scrolling panel (rows 1 to 3 are the header)
$define HM.DEPTH   8       ;* sub-menu pages open at most this many levels deep (MAX.DEPTH is int$keys.h's)

   common /tkhome/ hflag, hlogto

   prompt ''

   if @tty[1, 5] # '/dev/' then
      display sysmsg(11863)                             ;* no terminal: nothing here could be read as keys
      stop
   end
   hlogto = 0

   call $tk_open('home', '', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end

   is.admin = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)
   if is.admin then ctx<TK.C.AUD> = sysmsg(11803)

   cur.menu = ''                                          ;* the sub-menu page being shown (null: the top page); stk holds the pages left behind, crumb their names
   stk = ''
   crumb = ''
   ttl = 'Home'
   idx = 3                                                ;* the column of the identity (it moves right of the Back tile in a sub-menu)
   gosub make.keys

   X.COL =3 : @fm : 25 : @fm : 49 : @fm : 71 : @fm : 95 : @fm : 117      ;* the x of the six tile columns (a group of two stands at columns 1-2, 3-4 or 5-6)
   gen = 0
   top = 0
   fi = 1
   msg = ''
   outcome = ''
   done = 0
   lastmin = ''
   keep.id = ''
   keep.top = 0
   rc.on = 0                                              ;* 1 when the Recent group is on for this page (set by add.recent)

   aif = 0                                                ;* 1 while the AI line has the focus
   call $tk_ai('init', ctx, '', '')

   gosub geometry
   gosub build.page
   gosub layout
   gosub first.focus
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, ttl, msg)
      if aif then
         call $tk_ai('draw', ctx, 1, '')                     ;* the cursor is in the AI line while it has the focus
      end else
         call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)                  ;* the cursor waits at the start of the status line: in a window made smaller it is off the screen, and the library's cursor lock takes the keyboard
      end
      nm = ''
      screen key timeout 30 returning nm
      begin case
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
            gosub draw.clock
            gosub live.draw
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit                                          ;* the cursor lock's own way out
         case nm = 'resize'
            gosub relayout
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   gosub finish
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- how the program ends

finish:
   begin case
      case terminal.off and outcome # 'signout'
         * the Terminal tile is off for this account: the screen is not left for the prompt, whatever ended it (the cursor lock, the end of the input, a window too small
         * to take the screen again); the person is signed out
         if outcome = 'closed' then
            sleep 2                                       ;* the message that said why is on the screen; let it be read
         end else
            call $tk_close(ctx)
         end
         execute 'quit'
      case outcome = 'closed'
         null                                             ;* the screen was given back already (it could not be taken again)
      case outcome = 'terminal'
         call $tk_close(ctx)
         hflag = 1                                        ;* EXIT comes back here
         display sysmsg(11864)
      case outcome = 'signout'
         call $tk_close(ctx)
         execute 'quit'
      case 1
         call $tk_close(ctx)
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the geometry and the page

* The layout is the window when it is bigger than the minimum, the minimum when it is smaller (the frame's rule); the panel is the rows between the header and the hint line
geometry:
   lw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   lh = ctx<TK.C.H>
   py0 = PANEL.TOP
   py1 = lh - 5                                           ;* the hint line is row lh-4, the status line lh-3
   ph = py1 - py0 + 1
   return

* The tiles of this page.  The table is built for the audience (13.2): the administrator gets the administrator's, everyone else the holder's, and what a person may
* not use is not in memory.  Later apps add their rows here, in the commit that builds them.
build.page:
   * the tiles the administrator has turned off for this account (SET.TILE): left out of the page, their menu entries cannot be chosen
   call !home_off(@who, off.list)
   off.set = ' ' : off.list : ' '
   terminal.off = (index(off.set, ' terminal ', 1) > 0)
   tl = ''
   gr = ''
   pal.tools = (if is.admin then 'plum' else 'green')
   gname = (if is.admin then 'Tools' else 'My tools')
   bnd = 0                                                ;* the groups stand one band under another; a group that is not there takes no band
   g = 0
   if is.admin then
      * the administrator's own group: the page that manages what every account's home screen shows (it is in SDSYS's VOC only; an account holder's page has no such tile)
      bnd += 1
      g += 1
      gr<g> = 'System' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 2                 ;* the administrator's three groups stand side by side in one band, two tiles wide each, so that the page needs no scrolling
      id = 'menus' ; grp = g ; label = 'Menu management' ; glyph = '[=]' ; sub = 'tiles and start' ; act = 'cmd:tool.menus' ; pal = 'rust' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'viewers' ; grp = g ; label = 'Bypass programs' ; glyph = '[!]' ; sub = 'readers for pdf' ; act = 'cmd:tool.viewers' ; pal = 'rust' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'audit' ; grp = g ; label = 'Audit trail' ; glyph = '[*]' ; sub = 'who did what' ; act = 'cmd:tool.audit' ; pal = 'rust' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'config' ; grp = g ; label = 'Configuration' ; glyph = '[%]' ; sub = 'sd.conf and SD' ; act = 'cmd:tool.config' ; pal = 'rust' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      * who may do what, and who is on: the people and access group
      g += 1
      gr<g> = 'People and access' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 2
      id = 'accounts' ; grp = g ; label = 'Accounts' ; glyph = '(@)' ; sub = 'create and manage' ; act = 'cmd:tool.accounts' ; pal = 'amber' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'sessions' ; grp = g ; label = 'Sessions and locks' ; glyph = '[~]' ; sub = 'who is on' ; act = 'cmd:tool.sessions' ; pal = 'amber' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'gates' ; grp = g ; label = 'Gates' ; glyph = '[#]' ; sub = 'what accounts may do' ; act = 'cmd:tool.gates' ; pal = 'amber' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      * the data copies, the doors to other machines, and the AI
      g += 1
      gr<g> = 'Data, network and AI' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 2
      id = 'backups' ; grp = g ; label = 'Backups' ; glyph = '[<]' ; sub = 'save and restore' ; act = 'cmd:tool.backups' ; pal = 'blue' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'masters' ; grp = g ; label = 'Master files' ; glyph = '[M]' ; sub = 'shared copies' ; act = 'cmd:tool.masters' ; pal = 'blue' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'remote' ; grp = g ; label = 'Remote servers' ; glyph = '[>]' ; sub = 'doors and files' ; act = 'cmd:tool.remote' ; pal = 'blue' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      id = 'ai' ; grp = g ; label = 'AI' ; glyph = '(*)' ; sub = 'model and key' ; act = 'cmd:tool.ai' ; pal = 'violet' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   end
   bnd += 1
   g += 1
   gr<g> = gname : @vm : bnd : @vm : 6
   id = 'editor' ; grp = g ; label = 'Editor' ; glyph = '[=]' ; sub = 'edit a record' ; act = 'cmd:sed' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'ide' ; grp = g ; label = 'IDE' ; glyph = '</>' ; sub = 'programs and files' ; act = 'cmd:ide' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'ced' ; grp = g ; label = 'Record editor' ; glyph = '[ ]' ; sub = 'fields of a record' ; act = 'cmd:ced' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   * the person's own programs (MY.MENU), when the administrator has allowed it (the administrator always may): a group of their own after the standard tools, with a tile that
   * opens the list for changing.  They are only tiles that run what the person could type at their prompt.
   call !home_pins(@who, pins.on, pins.items)
   if pins.on then
      bnd += 1
      g += 1
      gr<g> = 'My programs' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 6
      id = 'mymenu' ; grp = g ; label = 'Add a program' ; glyph = '+  ' ; sub = 'change this list' ; act = 'cmd:my.menu' ; pal = 'teal' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      for pn = 1 to dcount(pins.items, @fm)
         id = 'pin' : pn ; grp = g ; label = pins.items<pn, 1> ; glyph = pins.items<pn, 2> ; sub = pins.items<pn, 3>[1, 19] ; act = 'cmd:' : pins.items<pn, 3>
         pal = 'teal' ; size = 'n' ; pause = pins.items<pn, 4> ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
      next pn
   end
   bnd += 1
   g += 1
   gr<g> = 'Everyone' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 6
   id = 'terminal' ; grp = g ; label = 'Terminal' ; glyph = '>_ ' ; sub = 'type exit to come back' ; act = 'terminal' ; pal = 'gray' ; size = 'w' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'keys' ; grp = g ; label = 'Keys' ; glyph = '^K ' ; sub = 'test your keyboard' ; act = 'cmd:tool.keys' ; pal = 'gray' ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   * the development tools, for every account in the account the person is in (plan 13.2: each app adds its tile in the commit that builds it); the last group, so that the others stay where they were
   bnd += 1
   g += 1
   gr<g> = 'Develop' : @vm : bnd : @vm : 6
   id = 'files' ; grp = g ; label = 'Files' ; glyph = '[F]' ; sub = 'files and indices' ; act = 'cmd:tool.files' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'voc' ; grp = g ; label = 'Vocabulary' ; glyph = '[V]' ; sub = 'verbs and pointers' ; act = 'cmd:tool.voc' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'dict' ; grp = g ; label = 'Dictionary' ; glyph = '[D]' ; sub = 'items and indices' ; act = 'cmd:tool.dict' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'query' ; grp = g ; label = 'Queries' ; glyph = '[Q]' ; sub = 'build a report' ; act = 'cmd:tool.query' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'bulk' ; grp = g ; label = 'Bulk update' ; glyph = '[B]' ; sub = 'change many records' ; act = 'cmd:tool.bulk' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'catalog' ; grp = g ; label = 'Programs' ; glyph = '[P]' ; sub = 'compile, catalogue' ; act = 'cmd:tool.catalog' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   id = 'test' ; grp = g ; label = 'Tests' ; glyph = '[T]' ; sub = 'run and judge tests' ; act = 'cmd:tool.test' ; pal = pal.tools ; size = 'n' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.tile
   * the header: two small tiles at the right, on screen rows 1 to 3
   hx = 95 ; hy = 1
   id = 'switch' ; grp = 0 ; label = 'Switch account' ; glyph = '<> ' ; sub = '' ; act = 'switch' ; pal = 'gray' ; size = 's' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.header
   hx = 117 ; hy = 1
   id = 'signout' ; grp = 0 ; label = 'Sign out' ; glyph = '-> ' ; sub = '' ; act = 'signout' ; pal = 'gray' ; size = 's' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.header
   if cur.menu # '' then
      * a sub-menu page: the way back, at the left end of the header, where the identity stood
      hx = 3 ; hy = 1
      id = 'back' ; grp = 0 ; label = 'Back' ; glyph = '<- ' ; sub = '' ; act = 'back' ; pal = 'gray' ; size = 's' ; pause = 0 ; why = '' ; gosub add.header
   end
   gosub add.recent
   gosub pick.level
   gosub live.read
   gosub alloc.styles
   gosub make.menus
   return

* The Recent group (the first group of the top page): the tiles the person started last, newest first, when they have turned it on (View menu) and the administrator has not turned it
* off for the account (SET.TILE account recent off: then nothing is read at all).  What the list keeps is an id: each recent tile is a copy of a tile of THIS table as it is now (a
* tile that is off, or that this page does not offer, is not there), so the list can start nothing the page does not.  rc.on says whether the group is on.
add.recent:
   rc.on = 0
   if index(off.set, ' recent ', 1) then return
   call !home_recent('get', rc.on, rc.ids)
   if not(rc.on) then return
   rc.tiles = ''
   for rk = 1 to dcount(rc.ids, @fm)
      for ri = 1 to nt
         if tl<ri, HT.ID> = rc.ids<rk> and tl<ri, HT.GROUP> > 0 and tl<ri, HT.ACT>[1, 4] = 'cmd:' then
            t = tl<ri>
            t<1, HT.ID> = 'r:' : tl<ri, HT.ID>
            t<1, HT.GROUP> = 1
            t<1, HT.SIZE> = 'n'
            rc.tiles<-1> = t
            exit
         end
      next ri
   next rk
   if rc.tiles = '' then return
   for ri = 1 to nt
      if tl<ri, HT.GROUP> > 0 then tl<ri, HT.GROUP> = tl<ri, HT.GROUP> + 1       ;* every group moves down one place; Recent is the first, in a band of its own before band 1
   next ri
   gr = 'Recent' : @vm : 0 : @vm : 6 : @fm : gr
   tl = rc.tiles : @fm : tl
   nt = dcount(tl, @fm)
   return

* Only the page being shown is kept.  A folder tile (action menu:<name>) whose menu holds no tile is left out first (leaving one out can empty the menu above it); then the groups
* of the menu cur.menu and the tiles of those groups stay, with the header tiles, and the groups are numbered again.
pick.level:
   loop
      dropped = 0
      for pi = nt to 1 step -1
         pa = tl<pi, HT.ACT>
         if pa[1, 5] = 'menu:' then
            pn = 0
            for pj = 1 to nt
               pg = tl<pj, HT.GROUP>
               if pg > 0 then
                  if gr<pg, HG.MENU> = pa[6, 99] then pn += 1
               end
            next pj
            if pn = 0 then
               del tl<pi>
               nt -= 1
               dropped = 1
            end
         end
      next pi
      if dropped = 0 then exit
   repeat
   gmap = ''
   gr2 = ''
   for pk = 1 to dcount(gr, @fm)
      if gr<pk, HG.MENU> = cur.menu then
         gr2<-1> = gr<pk>
         gmap<pk> = dcount(gr2, @fm)
      end
   next pk
   tl2 = ''
   for pi = 1 to nt
      pg = tl<pi, HT.GROUP>
      if pg = 0 then
         tl2<-1> = tl<pi>
      end else
         if gmap<pg> # '' then
            t = tl<pi>
            t<1, HT.GROUP> = gmap<pg>
            tl2<-1> = t
         end
      end
   next pi
   tl = tl2
   gr = gr2
   nt = dcount(tl, @fm)
   return

add.tile:
   added = 0
   if index(off.set, ' ' : id : ' ', 1) then return        ;* turned off by the administrator: not on the page at all
   t = id : @vm : grp : @vm : label : @vm : glyph : @vm : sub : @vm : act : @vm : pal : @vm : size : @vm : pause : @vm : why
   tl<-1> = t
   nt = dcount(tl, @fm)
   added = 1
   return

* A header tile: its place is fixed on the screen (hx, hy), and it does not scroll
add.header:
   gosub add.tile
   if not(added) then return
   tl<nt, HT.X> = hx
   tl<nt, HT.Y> = hy
   tl<nt, HT.W> = 21
   tl<nt, HT.H> = 3
   tl<nt, HT.FIXED> = 1
   return

* A style for each palette in use: the colours and the same reversed and bold for the tile that has the focus.  A terminal with no colour (the library says none) gets
* the tiles in boxes, reverse video for the focus: nothing here depends on colour.
alloc.styles:
   colour = 1
   pnames = ''
   pcode = ''
   pfocus = ''
   for i = 1 to nt
      p = tl<i, HT.PAL>
      locate p in pnames<1> setting k else
         pnames<-1> = p
         gosub palette.colours
         call $sl_theme('slot', pf, pb, '', '', c1)
         call $sl_theme('slot', pf, pb, 'reverse bold', '', c2)
         if c1 = 'none' or c1 = 'full' or c1 = 'bad' or c2 = 'none' or c2 = 'full' or c2 = 'bad' then
            colour = 0                                    ;* one style missing: the whole page is drawn plain, boxed
            c1 = 'normal'
            c2 = 'reverse'
         end
         pcode<-1> = c1
         pfocus<-1> = c2
      end
   next i
   return

* The eight colours of a terminal are all there are: the page's accents are the nearest of them
palette.colours:
   begin case
      case p = 'amber'
         pf = 'black' ; pb = 'brown'
      case p = 'rust'
         pf = 'white' ; pb = 'red'
      case p = 'olive'
         pf = 'black' ; pb = 'green'
      case p = 'plum'
         pf = 'white' ; pb = 'magenta'
      case p = 'blue'
         pf = 'white' ; pb = 'blue'
      case p = 'teal'
         pf = 'black' ; pb = 'cyan'
      case p = 'green'
         pf = 'black' ; pb = 'green'
      case p = 'violet'
         pf = 'white' ; pb = 'magenta'
      case 1
         pf = 'black' ; pb = 'white'                      ;* gray
   end case
   return

* The panel's rows: bands one under another, the groups of a band side by side, the tiles of a group flowing left to right and wrapping.  The panel row 1 is the first
* heading (row 6 of the screen).  ch is the height of the whole page.
layout:
   nb = 0
   b0 = 1                                                 ;* the first band: 1, or 0 when the Recent group is on the page
   ng = dcount(gr, @fm)
   for k = 1 to ng
      if gr<k, HG.BAND> > nb then nb = gr<k, HG.BAND>
      if gr<k, HG.BAND> < b0 then b0 = gr<k, HG.BAND>
   next k
   ys = 1
   for b = b0 to nb
      c0 = 0
      bandend = ys
      for k = 1 to ng
         gn.tiles = 0                                     ;* a group whose tiles are all off has no heading either
         for i = 1 to nt
            if tl<i, HT.GROUP> = k then gn.tiles += 1
         next i
         if gr<k, HG.BAND> = b and gn.tiles > 0 then
            gcols = gr<k, HG.COLS>
            gr<k, HG.Y> = ys
            gr<k, HG.X> = X.COL<c0 + 1>
            cc = 0
            ry = ys + 1
            rowh = 0
            for i = 1 to nt
               if tl<i, HT.GROUP> = k then
                  tw = (if tl<i, HT.SIZE> = 'w' then 2 else 1)
                  th = (if tl<i, HT.SIZE> = 's' then 3 else 5)
                  if cc + tw > gcols then
                     cc = 0
                     ry += rowh + 1
                     rowh = 0
                  end
                  tl<i, HT.X> = X.COL<c0 + cc + 1>
                  tl<i, HT.Y> = ry
                  tl<i, HT.W> = (if tw = 2 then 43 else 21)
                  tl<i, HT.H> = th
                  tl<i, HT.FIXED> = 0
                  cc += tw
                  if th > rowh then rowh = th
               end
            next i
            if ry + rowh > bandend then bandend = ry + rowh
            c0 += gcols
         end
      next k
      if c0 > 0 then ys = bandend + 1                     ;* a band with no group (a sub-menu's groups start at a later band, or all of a band is off) takes no room
   next b
   ch = ys
   if top > ch - ph then top = ch - ph
   if top < 0 then top = 0
   return

* fb: the first tile of a group (the first tile of the page when only the header has any)
find.first:
   fb = 1
   for i = 1 to nt
      if tl<i, HT.GROUP> > 0 then
         fb = i
         exit
      end
   next i
   return

first.focus:
   gosub find.first
   fi = fb
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   screen clear at 0,py0 size lw,ph
   gosub draw.header
   gosub draw.panel
   screen menubar menus row 0 draw else null
   if ctx<TK.C.AI> then
      call $tk_ai('draw', ctx, aif, '')
   end else
      screen text '' at 0,lh - 4 width lw
      screen text 'arrows move  -  Enter starts  -  type to find  -  PgDn next group' at 3,lh - 4 attr 'disabled'
   end
   return

draw.header:
   screen clear at 0,1 size 94,3                          ;* the left of the header: the identity moves right of the Back tile and left again
   if is.admin then
      who.line = 'administrator'
   end else
      who.line = @logname : ' @ ' : @who
   end
   screen text fmt(who.line, '60L') at idx,2 attr 'bold'
   gosub draw.clock
   for i = 1 to nt
      if tl<i, HT.FIXED> then
         di = i
         gosub draw.tile
      end
   next i
   return

* The date and the time, dim: written again when the minute changes (the key wait is 30 seconds)
draw.clock:
   mm = oconv(time(), 'MT')
   if mm # lastmin then
      lastmin = mm
      wd = downcase(oconv(date(), 'DWA'))
      wd[1, 1] = upcase(wd[1, 1])
      dt = oconv(date(), 'D4DMY[,A3]')
      mo = field(dt, ' ', 2)
      mo = upcase(mo[1, 1]) : downcase(mo[2, 9])
      screen text fmt(wd : ' ' : field(dt, ' ', 1) : ' ' : mo : ' ' : field(dt, ' ', 3) : '  -  ' : mm, '60L') at idx,3 attr 'disabled'
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- live lines

* A tile may carry one short live line in place of its sub line (plan 13.1).  Only the administrator's page has any: how many accounts there are, how many sessions are
* signed on, what the master files' journal holds.  Each is a question the page could ask on its own screen and each only reads.  They are read when the page is built
* (the first time and on F5) and when the key wait runs out (30 seconds); live.chg holds the tiles whose line is not the one it was.
live.read:
   live.chg = ''
   if not(is.admin) then return
   for i = 1 to nt
      lid = tl<i, HT.ID>
      if lid[1, 2] = 'r:' then lid = lid[3, 99]              ;* a recent tile is a copy and shows the live line of the tile it copies
      txt = ''
      begin case
         case lid = 'accounts'
            gosub live.accounts
         case lid = 'sessions'
            gosub live.sessions
         case lid = 'masters'
            gosub live.masters
      end case
      if txt # tl<i, HT.LIVE> then
         tl<i, HT.LIVE> = txt
         live.chg<-1> = i
      end
   next i
   return

live.accounts:
   n = 0
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to lf then
      select lf to 9
      loop
         readnext lacc from 9 else exit
         if lacc # 'sdsys' then n += 1
      repeat
      close lf
      txt = n : (if n = 1 then ' account' else ' accounts')
   end
   return

live.sessions:
   call !listu(ludata)
   n = dcount(ludata, @fm)
   txt = n : ' signed on'
   call !sdsysn(sdn, sdids, sdmine, sdtty)                      ;* S.76: SDSYS on a terminal in more than one place is said on the tile (the tile is 19 characters wide)
   if sdn > 1 then txt = n : ' signed, ' : sdn : ' sdsys'
   return

live.masters:
   ans = kernel(K$MASTERS, 'ready')
   if ans<2> # 1 then
      txt = 'not set up'
   end else
      ans = kernel(K$MASTERS, 'pending')
      if ans<1> = 0 and ans<4> > 0 then
         txt = ans<4> : (if ans<4> = 1 then ' line pending' else ' lines pending')
      end else
         txt = 'nothing pending'
      end
   end
   return

* The key wait ran out: read the lines again and draw only the tiles whose line changed
live.draw:
   gosub live.read
   for k = 1 to dcount(live.chg, @fm)
      di = live.chg<k>
      gosub draw.tile
   next k
   return

draw.panel:
   for k = 1 to ng
      gy = gr<k, HG.Y>
      if gy # '' then
         sy = py0 + gy - top
         if sy >= py0 and sy <= py1 then
            screen text fmt(gr<k, HG.NAME>, '40L') at gr<k, HG.X>,sy attr 'header' width 40
         end
      end
   next k
   for i = 1 to nt
      if tl<i, HT.FIXED> = 0 then
         di = i
         gosub draw.tile
      end
   next i
   gosub draw.scrollbar
   return

* One tile, row by row so that a tile only partly in the panel draws the rows that are
draw.tile:
   tx = tl<di, HT.X>
   tw = tl<di, HT.W>
   th = tl<di, HT.H>
   ty = tl<di, HT.Y>
   if tl<di, HT.FIXED> = 0 then ty = py0 + ty - top
   focused = (di = fi)
   if aif then focused = 0                               ;* the AI line has the focus: no tile does
   p = tl<di, HT.PAL>
   locate p in pnames<1> setting pk else pk = 1
   begin case
      case tl<di, HT.WHY> # ''
         sty = 'disabled'
      case colour and focused
         sty = pfocus<pk>
      case colour
         sty = pcode<pk>
      case focused
         sty = 'reverse'
      case 1
         sty = 'normal'
   end case
   for r = 0 to th - 1
      sy = ty + r
      lo = (if tl<di, HT.FIXED> then 0 else py0)
      hi = (if tl<di, HT.FIXED> then lh else py1)
      if sy >= lo and sy <= hi then
         if colour then
            begin case
               case th = 3
                  s = (if r = 1 then '  ' : tl<di, HT.GLYPH> : '  ' : tl<di, HT.LABEL> else '')
               case r = 1
                  s = '  ' : tl<di, HT.GLYPH>
               case r = 3
                  s = '  ' : tl<di, HT.LABEL>
               case r = 4
                  s = '  ' : (if tl<di, HT.WHY> # '' then tl<di, HT.WHY> else (if tl<di, HT.LIVE> # '' then tl<di, HT.LIVE> else tl<di, HT.SUB>))
               case 1
                  s = ''
            end case
         end else
            call $sl_line('h', 0, hc)
            call $sl_line('v', 0, vc)
            begin case
               case r = 0
                  call $sl_line('tl', 0, c1)
                  call $sl_line('tr', 0, c2)
                  s = c1 : str(hc, tw - 2) : c2
               case r = th - 1
                  call $sl_line('bl', 0, c1)
                  call $sl_line('br', 0, c2)
                  s = c1 : str(hc, tw - 2) : c2
               case th = 3
                  s = vc : fmt('  ' : tl<di, HT.GLYPH> : '  ' : tl<di, HT.LABEL>, (tw - 2) : 'L') : vc
               case r = 1
                  s = vc : fmt('  ' : tl<di, HT.GLYPH>, (tw - 2) : 'L') : vc
               case r = 2
                  s = vc : fmt('  ' : tl<di, HT.LABEL>, (tw - 2) : 'L') : vc
               case 1
                  s = vc : fmt('  ' : (if tl<di, HT.WHY> # '' then tl<di, HT.WHY> else (if tl<di, HT.LIVE> # '' then tl<di, HT.LIVE> else tl<di, HT.SUB>)), (tw - 2) : 'L') : vc
            end case
         end
         screen text s at tx,sy attr sty width tw
      end
   next r
   return

* The scroll bar in the last column, in the library's scroll style (dark grey in the colour themes), only when the page is taller than the panel
draw.scrollbar:
   if ch > ph then
      call $sl_scrollbar(ph, top + 1, ch, ph, bar)
      for r = 1 to ph
         screen text bar[r, 1] at lw - 1,py0 + r - 1 attr 'scroll'
      next r
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the focus

* Move the focus to tile j, scroll to keep it in the panel, and draw what changed
set.focus:
   if j < 1 or j > nt then return
   oldfi = fi
   fi = j
   oldtop = top
   gosub scroll.into.view
   if top # oldtop then
      screen clear at 0,py0 size lw,ph
      gosub draw.panel
      di = fi
      gosub draw.tile
      if tl<oldfi, HT.FIXED> then
         di = oldfi
         gosub draw.tile
      end
   end else
      di = oldfi
      gosub draw.tile
      di = fi
      gosub draw.tile
   end
   return

* The tile with its group's heading when it is the first row of its group
scroll.into.view:
   if tl<fi, HT.FIXED> then return
   ty = tl<fi, HT.Y>
   th = tl<fi, HT.H>
   fg = tl<fi, HT.GROUP>
   gy = gr<fg, HG.Y>
   first.row = (ty = gy + 1)
   want.top = (if first.row then ty - 2 else ty)       ;* the heading is the row above, with the blank row above that
   if want.top < 0 then want.top = 0
   if ty - (if first.row then 1 else 0) < top then
      top = want.top
   end else
      if ty + th - 1 > top + ph - 1 then top = ty + th - ph
   end
   if top > ch - ph then top = ch - ph
   if top < 0 then top = 0
   return

* The nearest tile in the direction dir: the distance along it, plus three times the distance across it
move.focus:
   best = 0
   bests = 1000000
   fx0 = tl<fi, HT.X>
   fx1 = fx0 + tl<fi, HT.W> - 1
   fy0 = tl<fi, HT.Y> - (if tl<fi, HT.FIXED> then py0 else 0)        ;* panel rows: a header tile is above the panel, so negative
   fy1 = fy0 + tl<fi, HT.H> - 1
   for j = 1 to nt
      if j # fi then
         jx0 = tl<j, HT.X>
         jx1 = jx0 + tl<j, HT.W> - 1
         jy0 = tl<j, HT.Y> - (if tl<j, HT.FIXED> then py0 else 0)
         jy1 = jy0 + tl<j, HT.H> - 1
         along = 0
         across = 0
         ov = 0
         ok = 0
         begin case
            case dir = 'right' and jx0 > fx1
               along = jx0 - fx1 ; across = abs(jy0 - fy0) ; ok = 1
               ov = (jy0 <= fy1 and jy1 >= fy0)
            case dir = 'left' and jx1 < fx0
               along = fx0 - jx1 ; across = abs(jy0 - fy0) ; ok = 1
               ov = (jy0 <= fy1 and jy1 >= fy0)
            case dir = 'down' and jy0 > fy1
               along = jy0 - fy1 ; across = abs(jx0 - fx0) ; ok = 1
               ov = (jx0 <= fx1 and jx1 >= fx0)
            case dir = 'up' and jy1 < fy0
               along = fy0 - jy1 ; across = abs(jx0 - fx0) ; ok = 1
               ov = (jx0 <= fx1 and jx1 >= fx0)
         end case
         if ok then
            sc = along + across + (if ov then 0 else 1000)           ;* a tile that shares rows (or columns) with this one comes before any that does not
            if sc < bests then
               bests = sc
               best = j
            end
         end
      end
   next j
   if best > 0 then
      j = best
      gosub set.focus
   end
   return

* The first tile of the next (dir = down) or previous group; a header tile has none
move.group:
   g = tl<fi, HT.GROUP>
   if g = 0 then return
   g += (if dir = 'down' then 1 else -1)
   if g < 1 or g > ng then return
   for j = 1 to nt
      if tl<j, HT.GROUP> = g then
         gosub set.focus
         return
      end
   next j
   return

* Reading order: the header first, then the groups
next.tile:
   j = fi + dir
   if j < 1 then j = nt
   if j > nt then j = 1
   gosub set.focus
   return

* A letter: the next tile, after this one, whose label begins with it
jump.letter:
   for n = 1 to nt
      j = fi + n
      if j > nt then j = j - nt
      if upcase(tl<j, HT.LABEL>[1, 1]) = upcase(nm) then
         gosub set.focus
         return
      end
   next n
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and the mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if aif then
      gosub ai.key
      return
   end
   begin case
      case nm = 'up' or nm = 'down' or nm = 'left' or nm = 'right'
         dir = nm
         gosub move.focus
      case nm = 'tab'
         dir = 1
         if ctx<TK.C.AI> and fi = nt then
            gosub ai.focus.on                              ;* the AI line is the last stop of the ring
         end else
            gosub next.tile
         end
      case nm = 'btab'
         dir = -1
         if ctx<TK.C.AI> and fi = 1 then
            gosub ai.focus.on
         end else
            gosub next.tile
         end
      case nm = 'home'
         gosub find.first
         j = fb
         gosub set.focus
      case nm = 'end'
         j = nt
         for i = nt to 1 step -1
            if tl<i, HT.GROUP> > 0 then
               j = i
               exit
            end
         next i
         gosub set.focus
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         dir = 'down'
         gosub move.group
      case nm = 'pgup'
         dir = 'up'
         gosub move.group
      case nm = 'enter' or nm = ' '
         gosub start.tile
      case nm = 'esc' or nm = 'bs'
         gosub close.menu                                  ;* back one page; on the top page there is nowhere to go and nothing happens
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub rebuild
      case nm = 'f10'
         gosub run.menu
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         gosub do.signout
      case len(nm) = 1 and nm > ' '
         gosub jump.letter
   end case
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   kind = mev<1>
   mx = mev<3>
   my = mev<4>
   begin case
      case kind = 'wheel'
         oldtop = top
         top += (if mev<2> = 'up' then -3 else 3)
         if top > ch - ph then top = ch - ph
         if top < 0 then top = 0
         if top # oldtop then
            screen clear at 0,py0 size lw,ph
            gosub draw.panel
         end
      case kind = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 and ctx<TK.C.AI> and my = lh - 4
         gosub ai.focus.on                                 ;* a click on the AI line gives it the focus
      case kind = 'press' and mev<2> = 1
         if my = 0 then
            screen menubar menus click mx returning mc then
               cmd = mc
               gosub run.cmd
            end
         end else
            for j = 1 to nt
               tx = tl<j, HT.X>
               ty = tl<j, HT.Y>
               if tl<j, HT.FIXED> = 0 then ty = py0 + ty - top
               in.rows = (my >= ty and my < ty + tl<j, HT.H>)
               if tl<j, HT.FIXED> = 0 then in.rows = (in.rows and my >= py0 and my <= py1)
               if in.rows and mx >= tx and mx < tx + tl<j, HT.W> then
                  gosub set.focus
                  gosub start.tile
                  exit
               end
            next j
         end
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the AI line

ai.focus.on:
   aif = 1
   di = fi
   gosub draw.tile                                       ;* the tile that had the focus is drawn without it
   call $tk_ai('focus', ctx, 1, '')
   msg = sysmsg(11638)
   return

* The tile that had the focus before the AI line took it has it again
ai.tile.back:
   di = fi
   gosub draw.tile
   return

* A key while the AI line has the focus: the line edits it; Esc, Tab, Back-tab, Up and Down give the focus back, and Enter on a request asks
ai.key:
   call $tk_ai('key', ctx, nm, out)
   begin case
      case out = 'leave'
         aif = 0
         msg = ''
         gosub ai.tile.back
      case out = 'tab'
         aif = 0
         j = 1                                            ;* round the ring: the first tile
         gosub set.focus
      case out = 'btab' or out = 'up'
         aif = 0
         j = nt                                           ;* back to the last tile
         gosub set.focus
      case out = 'down'
         aif = 0
         gosub ai.tile.back
      case out = 'ask'
         gosub ask.ai
   end case
   return

* The request in the line goes to $tk_ai with what this page can do: the tiles that start a tool (never Sign out or Switch account).  The answer is a tile to start or a command
* to run, each only after the person has chosen Accept or Run; both are done exactly as a click on a tile or the Terminal tile's prompt would do them.
ask.ai:
   acts = ''
   for i = 1 to nt
      ta = tl<i, HT.ACT>
      if ta[1, 4] = 'cmd:' or ta = 'terminal' then
         if tl<i, HT.ID>[1, 2] # 'r:' then                ;* a recent tile is a copy of one that is offered already
            acts<1, -1> = tl<i, HT.ID> : ':' : tl<i, HT.LABEL> : ' - ' : (if tl<i, HT.SUB> = '' then 'starts ' : ta else tl<i, HT.SUB>)
         end
      end
   next i
   ctxt = 'This is the home screen of the SD database system, a page of tiles.' : @vm : 'Each action starts the tool of that tile, exactly as the person could by choosing the tile.'
   ctxt := @vm : 'The person is ' : (if is.admin then 'the administrator.' else 'an account holder.')     ;* the lines of the page's text are VALUES (a field mark would move the fields after it)
   actx = 'home' : @fm : 'home' : @fm : ctxt : @fm : acts : @fm : 1
   call $tk_ai('ask', ctx, actx, res)
   call $tk_ai('clear', ctx, '', '')
   aif = 0
   msg = res<5>
   begin case
      case res<1> = 'action'
         found = 0
         for i = 1 to nt
            if tl<i, HT.ID> = res<2> then found = i
         next i
         if found then
            j = found
            gosub set.focus
            gosub start.tile
         end
      case res<1> = 'command'
         sentence = res<2>
         pause = 1
         keep.id = tl<fi, HT.ID>
         keep.top = top
         gosub run.command
         keep.id = ''
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what a tile does

start.tile:
   act = tl<fi, HT.ACT>
   begin case
      case act[1, 4] = 'cmd:'
         sentence = act[5, 9999]
         pause = tl<fi, HT.PAUSE>
         gosub note.recent
         gosub run.command
      case act[1, 5] = 'menu:'
         gosub open.menu
      case act = 'back'
         gosub close.menu
      case act = 'terminal'
         outcome = 'terminal'
         done = 1
      case act = 'switch'
         gosub switch.account
      case act = 'signout'
         gosub do.signout
   end case
   return

* The tile just started goes first in the Recent list, when the group is on for this page.  The id is what is kept (a recent tile's id is r: and the tile's own); the person's
* own programs (pin1, pin2 ...) are their own list already and are not kept here.  When the group is off nothing is asked of the file at all.
note.recent:
   if not(rc.on) then return
   rid = tl<fi, HT.ID>
   if rid[1, 2] = 'r:' then rid = rid[3, 99]
   if rid[1, 3] = 'pin' then return
   call !home_recent('add', rid, '')
   return

* The command is given the terminal: the screen is closed, the command runs as the person would have typed it, and the screen is taken again
run.command:
   keep.id = tl<fi, HT.ID>                               ;* the screen comes back with the same tile selected, scrolled as it was
   keep.top = top
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   execute sentence
   if pause then gosub wait.key
   gosub reopen
   keep.id = ''
   return

* The terminal is the ordinary one again here (the screen was closed), where a key is read when Enter is pressed: so the question is for Enter, and INPUT reads it
wait.key:
   crt
   crt sysmsg(11865) :
   input junk
   return

* Take the screen again after a command (or a LOGTO) and draw the page; the window may have changed, and the account may be another
reopen:
   call $tk_open('home', '', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      outcome = 'closed'
      done = 1
      return
   end
   is.admin = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)
   if is.admin then ctx<TK.C.AUD> = sysmsg(11803)
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   lastmin = ''
   aif = 0
   call $tk_ai('init', ctx, '', '')                       ;* the account may be another, and the window another size
   gosub geometry
   want.id = keep.id
   want.top = keep.top
   gosub enter.level
   return

* F5: the page again for what the session is now
rebuild:
   aif = 0
   call $tk_ai('init', ctx, '', '')                       ;* F5 also reads whether the AI is on now
   want.id = ''
   want.top = 0
   gosub enter.level
   msg = 'page built again'
   return

* The page of the menu being shown (cur.menu), built, laid out and drawn.  want.id (null for none) is the tile that has the focus and want.top how far the panel was scrolled when it
* had it: the page comes back as it was left, scrolled further only when that tile is out of the panel (a Recent group may have appeared above it).
enter.level:
   aif = 0
   gosub make.keys
   gosub set.title
   gosub build.page
   gosub layout
   gosub first.focus
   top = 0
   if want.id # '' then
      for i = 1 to nt
         if tl<i, HT.ID> = want.id then
            fi = i
            top = want.top
         end
      next i
      if top > ch - ph then top = ch - ph
      if top < 0 then top = 0
      gosub scroll.into.view
   end
   gosub draw.all
   return

* The key table: a sub-menu page also has Esc (back)
make.keys:
   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'start', 'start', '', 1)
   if cur.menu # '' then call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'back', 'back', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f10', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'sign out', 'signout', '', 1)
   return

* The status line's pane is the path of the page (Home > Develop), and the identity stands right of the Back tile on a sub-menu page
set.title:
   ttl = 'Home'
   for ck = 1 to dcount(crumb, @fm)
      ttl := ' > ' : crumb<ck>
   next ck
   idx = (if cur.menu # '' then 25 else 3)
   lastmin = ''                                          ;* the clock is written again where the identity now stands
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- sub-menus

* A folder tile (action menu:<name>): the menu opens as a page of its own.  What is left behind - the menu, the tile that had the focus and the scroll - is kept to give back.
* A menu that is already open above this one is refused (a page cannot open itself), and so is a ninth level.
open.menu:
   mname = act[6, 99]
   dep = dcount(stk, @fm)
   already = (mname = cur.menu or mname = '')
   for sk = 1 to dep
      if stk<sk, 1> = mname then already = 1
   next sk
   if already then
      msg = sysmsg(11956, mname)
      return
   end
   if dep >= HM.DEPTH then
      msg = sysmsg(11957, HM.DEPTH)
      return
   end
   stk<-1> = cur.menu : @vm : tl<fi, HT.ID> : @vm : top
   crumb<-1> = tl<fi, HT.LABEL>
   cur.menu = mname
   want.id = ''
   want.top = 0
   gosub enter.level
   return

* Back one page: the page left is built again with the focus and the scroll it had.  On the top page there is nothing to go back to.
close.menu:
   dep = dcount(stk, @fm)
   if dep = 0 then return
   e = stk<dep>
   cur.menu = e<1, 1>
   want.id = e<1, 2>
   want.top = e<1, 3>
   del stk<dep>
   del crumb<dep>
   gosub enter.level
   return

* View > Recent group: the person turns the group on (the file &menus& is made when it is not there) or off (the list is forgotten).  The administrator's SET.TILE ... recent off wins.
toggle.recent:
   if index(off.set, ' recent ', 1) then
      msg = sysmsg(11961)
      return
   end
   junk = ''
   rok = 0
   if rc.on then
      call !home_recent('off', rok, junk)
      rmsg = 11959
   end else
      call !home_recent('on', rok, junk)
      rmsg = (if rok then 11958 else 11960)
   end
   gosub rebuild
   msg = sysmsg(rmsg)
   return

* A resize: the screen was repainted under the frame
relayout:
   call $sl_window(w, h)
   lw = w
   lh = h
   if lw < TK.MINW then lw = TK.MINW
   if lh < TK.MINH then lh = TK.MINH
   ctx<TK.C.W> = lw
   ctx<TK.C.H> = lh
   ctx<TK.C.YSTAT> = lh - 3
   ctx<TK.C.YBORD> = lh - 2
   ctx<TK.C.YKEYS> = lh - 1
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   lastmin = ''
   aif = 0
   call $tk_ai('init', ctx, '', '')                       ;* the rows moved: the line is made again (its text is lost, a resize is rare)
   gosub geometry
   gosub layout
   gosub draw.all
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the menu bar

make.menus:
   menus = ''
   m = '&File|&Sign out~^Q~signout'
   gosub add.menu
   tflag = (if terminal.off then 'D' else '')                ;* D: the entry cannot be chosen (a tile that is off has no menu entry either)
   sflag = (if index(off.set, ' switch ', 1) then 'D' else '')
   kflag = (if index(off.set, ' keys ', 1) then 'D' else '')
   bflag = (if cur.menu = '' then 'D' else '')               ;* Back: only on a sub-menu page
   rflag = (if index(off.set, ' recent ', 1) then 'D' else '')
   m = '&Go|&Terminal~~terminal~' : tflag : '|S&witch account~~switch~' : sflag
   m := '|&Back~Esc~back~' : bflag
   gosub add.menu
   m = '&View|&Refresh~F5~refresh'
   m := '|Recent &group (' : (if rc.on then 'on' else 'off') : ')~~recent~' : rflag
   gosub add.menu
   m = '&AI|AI is off~~ai~D'
   gosub add.menu
   m = '&Help|&Keys~~keys~' : kflag
   gosub add.menu
   return

add.menu:
   m = change(m, '|', @vm)
   m = change(m, '~', @sm)
   menus<-1> = m
   return

run.menu:
   screen menubar menus returning mc then
      cmd = mc
      gosub run.cmd
   end
   return

* A menu entry does what its tile does
run.cmd:
   begin case
      case cmd = 'signout'
         gosub do.signout
      case cmd = 'terminal'
         outcome = 'terminal'
         done = 1
      case cmd = 'switch'
         gosub switch.account
      case cmd = 'refresh'
         gosub rebuild
      case cmd = 'back'
         gosub close.menu
      case cmd = 'recent'
         gosub toggle.recent
      case cmd = 'keys'
         sentence = 'tool.keys'
         pause = 0
         gosub run.command
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- sign out and switch account

do.signout:
   so.text = sysmsg(11866)
   so.btns = '&Sign out' : @vm : '&Cancel'                ;* Cancel is the one Enter chooses: a stray Enter never signs anyone out
   screen msgbox so.text title 'Sign out' buttons so.btns default 2 returning b else b = 0
   if b = 1 then
      outcome = 'signout'
      done = 1
   end else
      msg = ''
   end
   return

* The accounts this person may enter, by the rule LOGTO applies (the administrator any, anyone else the account's group; a suspended account and SDSYS never), then
* the screen of the one chosen.  The process cannot become another person: it runs as one Linux user (plan 13.4).
switch.account:
   alist = ''
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 11
      loop
         readnext aid from 11 else exit
         read arec from acc.f, aid then
            ok = (upcase(trim(arec<ACC$SUSPENDED>)) # 'SUSPENDED')
            if downcase(aid) = 'sdsys' then ok = 0
            if ok and not(is.admin) then ok = is_grp_member(@logname, arec<ACC$GROUP>)
            if ok then
               locate aid in alist<1> by 'AL' setting pos else
                  ins aid before alist<pos>
               end
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   if alist = '' then
      msg = 'no account to switch to'
      return
   end
   screen pick alist title 'Switch account' returning pk else pk = 0
   if pk = 0 then return
   acct = alist<pk>
   if acct = @who then
      msg = 'already in ' : acct
      return
   end
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   hlogto = 1
   execute 'logto ' : acct
   hlogto = 0
   cur.menu = ''                                          ;* the screen of the new account starts at its top page
   stk = ''
   crumb = ''
   gosub reopen
   if @who # acct then msg = sysmsg(11867, acct)
   return

end

